Feature: Data Standardization of delivery_dt field in f_order table

  Background:
    Given the SQL script path is "/Workspace/stg/scripts/f_order.sql"
    And the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the target table is "purgo_playground.purgo_playground.f_order"

  Scenario: Validate delivery_dt is in Decimal (38,0) format as yyyymmdd
    Given delivery_dt values in f_order table
     | delivery_dt   |
     | 20240910      |
     | 20230615      |
     | 20210101      |
    When the delivery_dt is extracted from f_order table
    Then ensure delivery_dt is a Decimal(38,0) type
    And validate delivery_dt format is correct yyyymmdd
    And no conversion is needed for delivery_dt

  Scenario Outline: Report error for invalid delivery_dt format
    Given delivery_dt values in f_order table
     | <delivery_dt> |
    When the delivery_dt is extracted with incorrect format
    Then convert delivery_dt to correct Decimal(38,0) format
    And raise error message "<error_message>"

    Examples:
     | delivery_dt | error_message                                     |
     | 2024-09-10  | "Incorrect format, conversion to Decimal required" |
     | 09/15/2024  | "Incorrect format, conversion to yyyymmdd required" |
     | NULL        | "delivery_dt is missing or null"                   |

  Scenario Outline: Convert and validate delivery_dt from string to Decimal(38,0)
    Given delivery_dt values from multiple test cases
     | delivery_dt |
     | "2024-09-10"|
     | "2024/09/10"|
     | "20240910"  |
    When delivery_dt is stored as string
    Then convert delivery_dt to Decimal(38,0) format
    And validate delivery_dt is formatted as yyyymmdd

    Examples:
     | delivery_dt |
     | "2024-09-10"|
     | "2024/09/10"|
     | "20240910"  |

  Scenario: Handle error conditions with specific messages
    Given delivery_dt values with potential errors
    When the delivery_dt validation fails
    Then capture the error details in dq_reports table
    And the error message should denote format or null issue
    And entries in dq_reports should have correct error mappings

  Scenario: Ensure all records are checked for delivery_dt format
    Given all records in the f_order table
    When extracting delivery_dt from each record
    Then verify each delivery_dt is Decimal(38,0)
    And formatted correctly as yyyymmdd
    And log any discrepancies for audit purposes
